  "status": "experimental-public-api-not-conformance-evidence",
  "notes": "The selected 2025 requirement calls for RTI and federate message-history buffers that permit lost messages to be resent after a connection fault. Fourteen bounded public-API TCK cases now exercise complementary paths: an RTI-to-federate Join result, a federate-to-RTI getFederateHandle request lost before RTI acceptance, and accepted successful responses for RegisterObjectInstance, CreateFederationExecutionWithMIM, ReserveObjectInstanceName, DeleteObjectInstance, UpdateAttributeValues, SendInteraction, EnableTimeRegulation, EnableTimeConstrained, TimeAdvanceRequest, TimeAdvanceRequestAvailable, NextMessageRequest, and NextMessageRequestAvailable that are lost and replayed. These cases do not establish replay for every message type or complete coverage of either peer's history buffer.",
